  "_commit": {
    "id": "0804d80863ff4a7a327afe374480f26ecdd93b5d",
    "author": "Chirag Parsania <chirag.parsania@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "Chirag Parsania <chirag.parsania@gmail.com>",
    "message": "Bump to 1.1.6: independent equivalence check, edgeR QL option, tximport fixes\n\nVerification\n- benchmark_vista_equivalence() now compares VISTA with reference\n  DESeq2/edgeR/limma pipelines that share none of VISTA's code, matched by\n  identifier; a test enforces the separation, and injected defects in\n  VISTA's own helpers must be reported.\n\nedgeR\n- New edger_test = c(\"LRT\", \"QL\") in create_vista(), run_edger_analysis(),\n  benchmark_vista_equivalence() and validate_vista_deep(). LRT stays the\n  default; calls that rely on it get a notice that QL becomes the default\n  in VISTA 1.4.0 (see ?VISTA-deprecated). The test used is recorded in\n  cutoffs(v)$edger_test and in the report.\n\nBug fixes\n- Untested genes were stored with pvalue = 1; they keep the engine's NA.\n- Filtering a consensus table on padj returned the union in intersection\n  mode.\n- DEG-count plots dropped comparisons with no DEGs.\n- limma MA plots used log10(log2-CPM + 1) on the x axis.\n- An explicit intercept in design_formula survived for edgeR and limma.\n- tximport abundance/length could be imported as counts; unscaled tximport\n  counts are now converted to lengthScaledTPM (matching tximport), with\n  tx2gene summarised as summarizeToGene() does.\n- DESeq2 now accepts estimated counts, rounded after a shared filter.\n- Negative values are refused; exact TPM/CPM or log-scale input warns.\n- RSEM TPM/FPKM columns could be imported as counts.\n\nAlso: provenance records VISTA, R and engine versions; the code-economy\nvignette computes its tallies; docs and NEWS updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
    "time": 1792557732
  },
